          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Loosely speaking, the
            %strong boundary
            of a subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            of topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            consists of those points in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            that are neither ‘fully in’
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            nor are ‘fully not in’
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#of_a_subset_of_a_topological_space Of a subset of a topological space
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subset X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %strong boundary
            or
            %strong frontier
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial S
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closure"} closure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar S
            minus its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interior"} interior
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mo ∘
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^\circ
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi S
                  %mo =
                  %mover
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo \
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∘
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\partial S = \bar S \backslash S^\circ
          %p
            Letting
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ¬
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg
            denote set-theoretic complementation,
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi S
                    %mo =
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mo ∘
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi S
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial S = \neg (S^\circ \cup (\neg S)^\circ)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∂
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial
            restricted to closed sets as an operation on closed sets, then it becomes a special case of the boundary operator on a
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-Heyting+algebra"} co-Heyting algebra
          %h3#of_a_manifold Of a manifold
          %p
            In a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold+with+boundary"} manifold with boundary
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            the boundary is the collection of points which do not have a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighborhood"} neighborhood
            diffeomorphic to an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+n-ball"} open n-ball
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#general General
          %p
            One reason behind the notation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∂
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial
            may be this (cf.
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-Heyting+boundary"} co-Heyting boundary
          #Leibniz.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y
              be topological spaces. Then for closed subsets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subseteq X
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \subseteq Y
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leibniz+rule"} Leibniz rule
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial (A \times B) = (\partial A \times B) \cup (A \times \partial B)
              holds.
          %p
            Notice the conclusion
            %em must
            fail if
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            are
            %em not
            closed, since in this case
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\partial A \times B) \cup (A \times \partial B)
            is not closed (it doesn’t include
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial A \times \partial B
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The interior operation preserves intersections, so
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mi B
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∘
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∩
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∘
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∘
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∩
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %msup
                        %mi B
                        %mo ∘
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A \times B)^\circ = ((A \times Y) \cap (X \times B))^\circ = (A^\circ \times Y) \cap (X \times B^\circ)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo ¬
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∘
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mo ¬
                      %msup
                        %mi B
                        %mo ∘
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\neg A^\circ \times Y) \cup (X \times \neg B^\circ)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ×
                        %mi B
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widebar{A \times B} = A \times B
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\partial A \times B) \cup (A \times \partial B)
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A, B
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+space"} connected
              open subsets of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \cap B
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial A = \partial B
              implies
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = B
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              is open, we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi B
                    %mo =
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∘
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi A
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \subseteq \neg \partial B = \neg \partial A = A^\circ \cup (\neg A)^\circ,
            %p
              where the right side is a disjoint union of open sets.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              is connected, so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊆
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∘
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \subseteq A^\circ
              or
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi A
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∘
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \subseteq (\neg A)^\circ \subseteq \neg A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \cap B
              is inhabited. So
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo ⊆
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∘
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \subseteq A^\circ \subseteq A
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subseteq B
          %h3#collar_neighbourhood_theorem Collar neighbourhood theorem
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifolds"} topological manifolds
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold+with+boundary"} with boudnary
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/collar+neighbourhood+theorem"} collar neighbourhood theorem
          %h2#some_ramifications Some ramifications
          %p
            The
            %a{:href => "#Leibniz"} Leibniz rule
            shows that the boundary operator is better behaved when restricted to the lattice of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subspace"} closed subsets
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-Heyting+algebra"} co-Heyting algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∂
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial
            (
            %a{:href => "#Zar27"}> Zarycki 1927
            ) on these, the so called
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-Heyting+boundary"} co-Heyting boundary
            operators.
          %p
            Since the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+of+subtoposes"} lattice of subtoposes
            of a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            carries a co-Heyting algebra structure, it becomes possible to define (co-Heyting) boundaries of subtoposes and thereby even boundaries of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+theory"} geometric theories
            that the subtoposes correspond to! Intuitively, such a boundary
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial T
            of a theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            consists of those geometric sequents that neither ‘fully follow’ from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            nor ‘fully contradict’
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %p
            The interior
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Int
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Int(\mathcal{E}_j)
            of a subtopos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}_j
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
            is defined in an exercise of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SGA"} SGA4
            as the largest
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subtopos"} open subtopos
            contained in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}_j
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∂
                  %msub
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial\mathcal{E}_j
            is then defined as the subtopos complementary to the (open) join of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+subtopos"} exterior subtopos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ext
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ext(\mathcal{E}_j)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Int
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Int(\mathcal{E}_j)
            in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+of+subtoposes"} lattice of subtoposes
          %p
            The co-Heyting algebra perspective and the accompanying
            %em mereo-logic of theories
            was proposed by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"} William Lawvere
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-Heyting+boundary"} co-Heyting boundary
            for further pointers!
